<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Compound proportion by the ratio method</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\({@w1@}\) workers lay \({@k1@}\) m of drainage pipe in \({@d1@}\) days. How many days would \({@w2@}\) workers take to lay \({@k2@}\) m, working at the same rate? Use the ratio method.</p><p>(a) The change in length multiplies the number of days by [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) The change in the number of workers multiplies the number of days by [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>(c) Days needed: [[input:ans3]] days [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p><p>Give (a) and (b) as fractions, for example <code>3/4</code>, or as decimals correct to 3 decimal places; give (c) exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Change one quantity at a time and ask whether the answer gets bigger or smaller.</p><p>(a) Length: \({@k1@}\) m to \({@k2@}\) m. {@kw1@} pipe needs {@kw2@} days, so the factor is {@kw3@} than 1: \(\dfrac{ {@k2@} }{ {@k1@} } = {@fr(fk)@}\).</p><p>(b) Workers: \({@w1@}\) to \({@w2@}\). {@ww1@} workers need {@ww2@} days, so the factor is {@ww3@} than 1: \(\dfrac{ {@w1@} }{ {@w2@} } = {@fr(fw)@}\).</p><p>(c) Days \(= {@d1@} \times {@fr(fk)@} \times {@fr(fw)@} = {@dd(Dd)@}\).</p><p>Check by the unitary method: the job rate is \({@k1@} \div ({@w1@} \times {@d1@}) = {@fr(k1/(w1*d1))@}\) m per worker-day, and \({@k2@} \div ({@w2@} \times {@fr(k1/(w1*d1))@}) = {@dd(Dd)@}\) days.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[kgrp(n) := block([s, out, k], s: string(n), k: slength(s), if k < 5 then s else (out: "", while k > 3 do (out: sconcat("\\,", substring(s, k-2, k+1), out), k: k-3), sconcat(substring(s, 1, k+1), out)));
ksh(v) := block([c, w, f], c: floor(100*v+1/2), w: floor(c/100), f: c-100*w, if f = 0 then kgrp(w) else sconcat(kgrp(w), ".", if f < 10 then "0" else "", string(f)));
dd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else if integerp(1000*v) then dispdp(float(v),3) else dispdp(float(v),4);
fr(v) := if integerp(v) then string(v) else sconcat("\\frac{", string(num(v)), "}{", string(denom(v)), "}");
r1(v) := floor(10*v+1/2)/10;
ix: 1+rand(10);
/* Design: compound proportion by the ratio method. Source: original. Core only. [w1, k1, d1, w2, k2]: w1 workers lay k1 m of pipe in d1 days; w2 workers lay k2 m. Length grows in 5 entries and shrinks in 5; workers rise in 5 and fall in 5. Curated list, one seed per entry. */
L: [[12,360,10,15,540],[9,420,8,12,280],[20,500,9,15,750],[10,300,12,8,250],[8,240,6,12,480],[15,600,8,10,450],[6,180,9,9,360],[20,900,6,16,600],[14,560,5,10,640],[18,540,12,24,450]];
E: L[ix];
w1: E[1]; k1: E[2]; d1: E[3]; w2: E[4]; k2: E[5];
fk: k2/k1;
fw: w1/w2;
Dd: d1*fk*fw;
/* diagnostics */
wdir: d1*fk/fw;
linv: d1*fw/fk;
binv: d1/(fk*fw);
kup: is(k2>k1);
wup: is(w2>w1);
kw1: if kup then "More" else "Less";
kw2: if kup then "more" else "fewer";
kw3: if kup then "greater" else "less";
ww1: if wup then "More" else "Fewer";
ww2: if wup then "fewer" else "more";
ww3: if wup then "less" else "greater";
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
